# Reviewed history findings for scripts/history-secret-scan.mjs (SEC-05, 2026-10-23).
#
# Format:  <rule> <path> <fingerprint|-> [reason]
#
#   <fingerprint>  first 12 hex of SHA-256(secret). Safe only for a HIGH-ENTROPY value:
#                  an 8-character key or an email address can be recovered from a hash,
#                  so those use `-` instead.
#   -              any value of this rule at this path. Costs path-level precision; it is
#                  the last resort, and the reason has to say why a hash would disclose
#                  the value. A reviewer must be able to act on every `-` entry.
#
# Everything here was read and classified in HistorySecretScan.md. Nothing in this file is
# a secret: the two real findings are described, not reproduced, and their fingerprints are
# either withheld (`-`) or belong to a value long enough that a hash cannot be reversed.
# A finding that is NOT listed here fails the `history-secrets` CI job.

# ── real, removed from the tree but permanent in history ─────────────────────────────────
authorization-bearer-literal docs/DEVIN-CONNECT-CUTOVER.md - REAL: downstream gateway key (8 chars) in a curl example; redacted from the tree in 413106e, still in every clone. No fingerprint because a short lowercase key is recoverable from a 12-hex hash. Owner action: confirm the key was rotated.
openai-api-key scripts/model-identity-test.js fa682d4bfa18 REAL-LOOKING: default --api-key value for the model-identity script (37 chars, random core), removed in 14ad336 when the script started requiring an explicit key. Owner action: confirm and rotate if it was live.

